  "body": "Found by the QA swarm round 2 (#2582), brief q07 (MDF router part), CamCraft **v0.25.0** Linux x86_64 release, machine Sienci AltMill 4x4, post grblHAL.\n\n## What happens\n\nFour operations in one setup all use T1 (Router up-cut 6 mm). Between each pair the post stops the spindle, goes to machine Z0 and asks for the same tool again:\n\n```\nG0 X221.25 Y85 Z25\nM5\n(OPERATION: ThroughHoles - BORE - G54)\nG17 G90 G54 G40 G80\n(T1 Router up-cut 6 mm - FLAT END MILL D6)\nG53 G0 Z0\nT1 M6\nS18568 M3\n```\n\nOn a manual-tool-change grblHAL router, `M6` pauses the program (and can start a tool-length probe), so this job stops 3 extra times for a tool that is already in the spindle. The Tormach post had the same problem and keeps the tool since #1626. `assets/posts/grblhal.cps` on main still has no same-tool check.\n\n## Expected\n\nA section that keeps the previous section's tool writes no M5 / tool change / M6 (spindle and coolant words only if they change), as tormach.cps does.\n\n## Repro files\n\n- [q07-router.camproj](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q07-router-mdf/q07-router.camproj), posted [q07-router.nc](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/qa-artifacts/qa/round2-20261122/q07-router-mdf/q07-router.nc) (lines 48-55, 288-294, 371-377).\n- MCP: `open_project`, then `post {\"post\": \"grblHAL\", \"output\": \"...\"}`.\n\nDone means: grblhal.cps writes one T1 M6 for consecutive same-tool operations (pinned by a post golden with two operations on one tool), and the same check is made for the other grbl-family posts (Grbl 1.1, TinyG) or each says it is not needed.\n",
